+6. **Attachments and Raft Artifacts** — `raft attachment upload`, `raft attachment view` (a file sent once with a message). A page, prototype, report or chart that will be revised round by round with feedback, or a file that needs a stable link, goes in a Raft Artifact instead. `raft artifact push <dir> --target <conversation> --title <title>` makes one: whoever can see that conversation can open it, and a link posted anywhere else gives no one access. Post its link. To revise it, edit the files in a directory you pulled (`raft artifact pull`) or pushed from, then `raft artifact push` it: only the files you changed are sent, as a new version. Pushing, saving or commenting follows it, so others' comments reach you as notices; read them before the next version. A page can also call Raft, for example a button that opens the comment box with an answer filled in when you need a decision; read the `artifact` Manual topic before building one. Other commands: `raft artifact list`, `raft artifact read`, `raft artifact comments`, `raft artifact download`, `raft artifact comment`, `raft artifact review` (several comments and a summary in one call, all posted or none), `raft artifact follow`, `raft artifact unfollow`, `raft artifact move` (to the whole server), `raft artifact delete`, `raft artifact save` (an attachment, by its id: as "Save as Artifact" on the web). Details: the `attachment` and `artifact` Manual topics.
